WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.200
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.400
Here at "The Tonight Show,"
we love songs

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.434
and we especially love songs
written by our audience members

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:08.734
in under an hour.

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:11.100
It's time for "Battle of the
Instant Songwriters."

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.334
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:15.033
-♪ Singing a song,
and I'm singing a song ♪

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:20.067
♪ And I'm writing a song
about another song ♪

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:22.467
-Welcome to "Battle of the
Instant Songwriters."

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:24.534
Before the show, we went through
our audience and picked out

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:27.567
two people who said that
they were musicians.

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:30.801
We gave them each a made-up
song title and gave them an hour

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:33.434
to write an original song
based on that title.

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:36.033
Here's a shot of them practicing
backstage a minute ago.

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:37.567
This is real. Yeah.

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:39.534
Let's see what they came up with
and meet them right now.

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:41.434
Come on over, guys.
Welcome.

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:43.601
Hi.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:44.934
Nice to see you.
-Nice to see you.

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:46.534
-Hi. Welcome. Nice to see you.
-Hi. Thank you.

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:47.667
-Welcome to the show.

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:49.033
Let's start
with contestant number one.

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:50.234
What is your name and where
are you from?

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:52.501
-My name is Miranda.
I'm from Dallas, Texas.

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:57.434
-Hey! We love Dallas, Texas.
Big Dallas, Texas fan. Yeah.

00:00:57.434 --> 00:00:58.734
Welcome to the show.

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:01.234
What title were you given?
What title of the song?

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:04.000
-"Sweater Weather Love Letter."
-Ooh!

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.634
So we kind of gave you
a rhyme already.

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:07.534
Yeah, made it
real easy for you. Yeah.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.400
"A Sweater Weather"...

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.367
"Sweater Weather Love Letter."
-"Love Letter."

00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:12.634
-Yeah, perfect.

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:13.701
And what instrument
will you be playing tonight?

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:15.067
-Piano.
-Oh, beautiful.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:18.501
Alright, go up and get ready
and get in your headspace.

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:19.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:21.567
This will be exciting here.

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:23.033
And now, ladies and gentlemen,
here to perform

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:25.234
the world premiere
of the soon-to-be classic

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:29.634
"Sweater Weather Love Letter,"
it's Miranda Contreras-Peterson.

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:31.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:35.367
-♪ I take myself to town ♪

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:39.133
♪ And I take a look around ♪

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:42.767
♪ Oh, the leaves have
all changed ♪

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:50.434
♪ Like flames before my eyes ♪

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:51.968
Thank you.

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:54.734
♪ This is an ode to autumn ♪

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:57.267
♪ A nod to fall ♪

00:01:57.267 --> 00:02:02.234
♪ A song for my coat
that hangs on the wall ♪

00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:07.133
♪ And the candles I light
to brighten the halls ♪

00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:12.434
♪ It's a sweater-weather
love letter ♪

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:15.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:19.701
♪ It's a poem for my heart
that keeps me warm ♪

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:24.200
♪ Until I get to go back home ♪

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:29.200
♪ Like birds of a feather,
we will flock together ♪

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:34.534
♪ And share
our stories and our sweaters ♪

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:36.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:39.834
-Whoo-whoo!
-Thank you.

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:41.868
-Ooh, I love that!

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:44.334
Give it up for Miranda,
everybody.

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:46.467
That was incredible.

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:49.901
Whoo! Let's meet
contestant number two.

00:02:49.901 --> 00:02:51.501
What is your name and
where are you from?

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:54.767
-My name is Oren Levin, and I'm
from Ann Arbor, Michigan.

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:56.534
-Hey, Oren!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:56.534 --> 00:02:59.000
Ann Arbor. Shout-out
to Ann Arbor, Michigan.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:02.234
Alright, Oren, tell everyone
what your song title is.

00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:04.601
-My song title
was very different.

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:08.467
It was "Cranberry Sauce
Isn't a Sauce."

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:09.801
-What instrument
are you playing?

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:11.267
-I'm playing the guitar.
The acoustic guitar.

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:13.300
-Alright, buddy. Oren, go over
and get the guitar on,

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.634
and I'll introduce you.

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:17.000
Come over here, Miranda.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:22.567
Ladies and gentlemen, get ready
for the world premiere of

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:27.267
"Cranberry Sauce Isn't Even
a Sauce" by Oren Levin.

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:31.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:33.801
-♪ Now, I'm a lover of sauces ♪

00:03:33.801 --> 00:03:35.834
♪ Mustard, pesto, no conflict ♪

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:40.067
♪ A.1. or glaze from a pen ♪

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:42.868
♪ But with Thanksgiving
coming up ♪

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:45.000
♪ There's just one
heinous enough ♪

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.834
♪ To come right out of a can ♪

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:58.467
♪ I know it takes some time
to chew turkey that's dry ♪

00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:01.701
♪ But I'd rather dip it in ranch
than use a lump ♪

00:04:01.701 --> 00:04:03.234
♪ What is that stuff? ♪

00:04:03.234 --> 00:04:05.634
♪ Don't know what to call it ♪

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:09.534
♪ But sauce,
it shouldn't be solid.

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:17.567
♪ Oh, cranberry sauce
isn't even a sauce ♪

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:22.200
♪ Yeah, cranberry sauce
isn't even a sauce ♪

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.434
♪ It's shaped like a can ♪

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:26.367
♪ It comes out of a tube ♪

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:29.234
♪ Yeah, yeah, cranberry sauce ♪

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.100
♪ Yeah, I know that
I'm screwed ♪

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:38.434
♪ 'Cause I'm a saucy dude ♪

00:04:38.434 --> 00:04:42.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:46.067
Get over here! Come on!

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:48.467
-Saucy dude.
-He's a saucy dude.

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:51.367
Not bad. That was a good setup.
There you go.

00:04:51.367 --> 00:04:52.968
Give it up
for Oren once again.

00:04:52.968 --> 00:04:55.434
That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:57.033
Alright, now we're
going to see who won.

00:04:57.033 --> 00:05:00.133
We're going to let our great
audience decide the winner.

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:03.100
Yes. Was it Miranda?

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:06.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:08.267
Or was it Oren?

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:10.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:13.033
We're going to give it to Oren.
Congratulations.

00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:16.968
Oren is the winner.
You get -- Congratulations.

00:05:16.968 --> 00:05:19.501
You get this
"I love music" sweatshirt.

00:05:19.501 --> 00:05:21.133
Congratulations.
-I do love music.

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:24.000
-Yes, and that's for you.
-Amazing!

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:28.767
You also get a "Tonight Show"
notebook for writing more songs.

00:05:28.767 --> 00:05:31.267
And you get $1,000, as well.

00:05:31.267 --> 00:05:35.267
Thank you. Congratulations.
-Appreciate it.

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:37.100
-But no one goes home
empty-handed.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.067
Our other contestant
will receive an

00:05:39.067 --> 00:05:41.434
"I love music" sweatshirt,
as well.

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:43.667
-I do! Awesome.

00:05:43.667 --> 00:05:46.167
-And a "Tonight Show" notebook
and a $1,000.

00:05:46.167 --> 00:05:47.767
-Oh!
-There you go.

00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:49.334
-Oh! Everybody's a winner.

00:05:49.334 --> 00:05:52.367
-Yes. Give it up for your new
instant songwriters.

00:05:52.367 --> 00:05:55.100
Stick around. We'll be
right back with Jared Leto!

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:58.300
Come on back, everybody!
Well done.

